WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.320
- [Narrator] If you've
taken a menthol cough drop,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.370
you probably noticed a minty flavor

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.310
and a cool numbing sensation
in the back of your throat.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.050
That feeling is similar to the one you get

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.730
from smoking these, menthol cigarettes,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.730
and it's part of why
the Biden administration

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.020
is trying to prevent them from being sold.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.870
- Health officials say

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.550
that menthol cigarettes are
more appealing to young people

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.940
because the menthol eases
the throat irritation

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.050
that you experience when
you first try a cigarette.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.830
- [Narrator] Aside from regular tobacco,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.790
menthols are currently the only
flavor of cigarette allowed

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.960
on the market.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.290
And they're popular.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.570
43% of smokers in the US
used menthols in 2020.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.230
Here's why the FDA wants to ban them

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.100
from being sold and distributed in the US,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.590
and why the move is being opposed

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.300
by some Black community leaders.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.690
Menthol, a compound that
occurs naturally in mint plants

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.490
triggers the same receptors we use

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:50.560
to sense cold,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.870
which creates that numb,
chilling sensation.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.460
Menthol brands like Newport,

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.410
the most popular menthol in the US,

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.908
emphasized the flavor in
their older marketing.

00:00:59.908 --> 00:01:02.038
♪ Smoother Newport ♪

00:01:02.038 --> 00:01:03.949
♪ Fresher Newport ♪

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:06.575
♪ Smoother, more refreshing cigarette ♪

00:01:06.575 --> 00:01:08.110
- [Narrator] But the FDA
says that in addition

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.120
to reducing the harshness of smoking,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.390
menthol also makes it harder to quit.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.180
- Menthol interacts with nicotine

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.060
in the brain to enhance
nicotine's addictive effect,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.650
according to the FDA,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.480
making menthol cigarettes
even more additive

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.040
than regular cigarettes.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.910
So they start kids younger

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.750
and then they keep them
hooked for a lifetime,

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.060
US officials say.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.730
- [Narrator] The biggest
US tobacco companies

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.820
have rejected the FDA's findings.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.360
- They say that menthol cigarettes

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.860
don't have any different health effect

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.960
than a regular cigarette.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.370
- [Narrator] Despite this, the
FDA got White House support

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.320
to move forward on the ban last year

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.940
as part of the Biden administration's

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.570
Cancer Moonshot initiative,

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.330
which aims to reduce the cancer death rate

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.910
by at least 50% over the next 25 years.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.530
- The rules announced today
would enforce regulations

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.290
related to what stores sell

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.530
and what companies
manufacture and distribute.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.820
- [Narrator] A recent study projected

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.670
that a ban on menthol cigarettes

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.190
would prompt an estimated 1.3
million US smokers to quit.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.220
The FDA says that menthol smoking

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.930
disproportionately impacts
youth and young adults.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.200
In 2019, researchers estimated

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.240
that more than one million US middle

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.240
and high school students
had smoked a cigarette

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.670
in the last month.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.622
Of those, about 47%
reported smoking a menthol.

00:02:26.622 --> 00:02:30.380
The flavor is also popular
among Black smokers.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.180
- For decades, cigarette companies

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.760
have marketed menthol brands

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.610
like Newport, Kool and
Salem to Black people,

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:40.690
distributing free packs
in Black neighborhoods

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:43.060
and running magazine and billboard ads,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.480
depicting carefree Black smokers.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.230
- [Narrator] Black smokers are
more likely to use menthols.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.870
They also die at higher rates

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.100
of smoking-related
cancers than other groups,

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.960
according to the CDC.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.740
And US health officials say the ban

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.080
would help address those disparities.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.020
The NAACP has been in support of the ban,

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.910
saying that "the targeting and marketing

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:03.940
of menthol flavoring

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.460
by the tobacco industry

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.480
have had a devastating
impact on our community."

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.160
But others think the ban
could present problems.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.310
Reynolds American, which makes Newport,

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.880
has given money to prominent
Black community leaders

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.330
who have opposed the ban,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.610
like Reverend Al Sharpton

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.730
and Civil Rights attorney Ben Crump.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.240
Crump says he's accepted money

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.960
from Reynolds for things like scholarships

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.070
for Black youth

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.820
but the money has not
influenced his opinion.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.520
Sharpton did not reply
to requests for comment.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.560
They, and groups like the ACLU

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.630
and members of the
Congressional Black Caucus

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.460
have expressed concerns that the ban

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.210
will disproportionately
impact people of color.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.670
- They have argued that menthol bans

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.590
would lead to racial profiling

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.830
by police and expand the
illicit market for cigarettes.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.594
- [Narrator] In a statement
to The Wall Street Journal,

00:03:49.594 --> 00:03:51.780
Reynolds said, "It's important to note

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.920
that we do not make
contributions conditional

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.250
upon organizations maintaining
a particular position."

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.900
The Biden administration has said

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.240
that enforcement of a ban

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.610
would target manufacturers and sellers.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.660
- This is not about going

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.810
after individuals smoking
menthol cigarettes.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:07.210
This is about manufacturers

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.720
and people who are selling them.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:09.710
- [Narrator] Tobacco companies

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.760
could lose significant profits
if the ban is enforced.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.950
- They already have been grappling

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.680
with declining smoking rates in the US

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.620
and they are racing to develop

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.360
and market alternative products,

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.300
like e-cigarettes, nicotine pouches,

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.400
lozenges, and other alternatives

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.090
in the hopes that smokers
will switch over to those.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.970
- [Narrator] Even as smoking declines,

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.970
menthols remain a huge part
of the cigarette market.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:41.020
They account for about 1/3 of
all cigarettes sold in the US.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.960
British American Tobacco,
which makes Reynolds American,

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.240
and Altria, which makes Marlboro

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.500
are the top menthol makers in the US.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.420
Menthol makes up roughly 30%

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:53.330
of British American
Tobacco's global profits.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.770
Altria said in a statement

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.400
that it believes harm
reduction, not prohibition,

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.340
is the better path forward.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.920
Reynolds and Altria have
hinted that they may sue

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.860
if the ban goes into effect.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:07.400
- Litigation could tie this up for years.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.400
So even if the FDA moved forward

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.400
and set an effective
date of let's say 2024,

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.280
once that ban were implemented,

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.380
then the cigarette
companies would likely sue

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.050
and hold it up further.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.610
- [Narrator] The FDA
will hear public comments

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.850
on its proposed rules

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.600
and will take time to review
before finalizing the ban.

